  "query_preview": "..Monsoon moisture in place will finally have a\ntrigger mechanism acting on it as a trough brushes by. While most\nof the trough remains to the north, the southern edge will be\nclose enough to generate some showers and thunderstorms across\nArizona. Short term models are showing showers in areas north of \nInterstate 40 in the morning through the afternoon with areas \nprimarily east of Interstate 17 firing off in the afternoon.\nThings look like they may remain active into the night time hours\nover eastern Arizona as the trough moves through. Typical monsoon\nhazards will be in place, mainly frequent lightning, gusty winds,\nheavy rain and the potential for some isolated flash flooding.\n\nOn Saturday this first trough moves through the area taking its\ndynamics with it. Enough moisture will remain in place Saturday\nand Sunday for isolated to scattered thunderstorms over the\nhighest elevations with terrain influence and daytime heating\nbeing the main triggers.  \n\nStarting Sunday night and lasting through Wednesday a series of\ntroughs move through, each interacting with the monsoon moisture\nstill over the area. This will bring more widespread shower and\nthunderstorm chances each afternoon Monday through Wednesday.\n\nAfter the trough moves through Wednesday models are showing some\ndrying behind that trough that could potentially bring a dry spell\nstarting Thursday and lasting through the weekend. Will keep\nmonitoring to see if that indeed holds out.",
